(6096886, 895912, 28564, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Covert_Oddity:</b></div><hr/><i> This is a surprise shot from you, I was fully expecting you to be on the front page this challenge with one of your superb auto / ruined building shots.<br/> <br/>That being said, this is a really nice portrait, which for me fits the challenge nicely, I''m surprised it didn''t finish a lot higher, and I can''t really offer an explination why. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>the first thing i did this morning was to search the Jeb photo in this challenge, surprisingly, like Cover_Oddity says, is not a ruined building shot, but is a really good portrait that is not in a right place for me, an higher position would be better for this.<br/> <br/>my is a poor shot that is in the middle of classification, i do not expected a better place.</td>', 'Originally posted by Covert_Oddity: This is a surprise shot from you, I was fully expecting you to be on the front page this challenge with one of your superb auto / ruined building shots. That being said, this is a really nice portrait, which for me fits the challenge nicely, I''m surprised it didn''t finish a lot higher, and I can''t really offer an explination why.   the first thing i did this morning was to search the Jeb photo in this challenge, surprisingly, like Cover_Oddity says, is not a ruined building shot, but is a really good portrait that is not in a right place for me, an higher position would be better for this. my is a poor shot that is in the middle of classification, i do not expected a better place.', '2010-07-19 04:22:04.000000', NULL, 0),
